# ⌐◨-◨ NOUNS TERMINAL — Raspberry Pi Deployment Guide

## Overview

The Nouns Terminal is a GameBoy-inspired Nouns DAO governance client designed for a Raspberry Pi 3B+ with a 3-inch JJN Electron touchscreen + stylus. It provides:

- **Pixel Studio** — 32×32 pixel art editor using the Nouns on-chain color palette
- **Governance** — Browse proposals, vote FOR/AGAINST/ABSTAIN, view vote bars
- **Live Auction** — See current Noun auction, place bids
- **Candidates** — Browse proposal candidates, submit your pixel art as a candidate
- **Gallery** — View/manage your saved pixel artworks
- **Wallet** — Connect via WalletConnect or injected provider

---

## Architecture

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────┐
│          NOUNS TERMINAL (React)         │
│  ┌──────┐ ┌────────┐ ┌──────────────┐  │
│  │Studio│ │Governance│ │  Auction     │  │
│  │32×32 │ │Proposals │ │  Live Feed   │  │
│  │Editor│ │Voting    │ │  Bid UI      │  │
│  └──────┘ └────────┘ └──────────────┘  │
│  ┌──────────────────────────────────┐   │
│  │   ethers.js / viem / wagmi       │   │
│  │   Contract Interactions Layer    │   │
│  └──────────────────────────────────┘   │
│  ┌──────────────────────────────────┐   │
│  │   Nouns Subgraph (The Graph)     │   │
│  │   + Direct RPC for writes        │   │
│  └──────────────────────────────────┘   │
└─────────────────────────────────────────┘
         │                    │
    Ethereum RPC         Nouns Subgraph
    (Infura/Alchemy)     (The Graph)
```

---

## Hardware Setup

### Required Components
- Raspberry Pi 3B+ (or 4)
- JJN Electron 3-inch touchscreen (480×320 or similar)
- Stylus (for precise pixel art)
- MicroSD card (16GB+)
- Power supply (5V 2.5A)

### Touchscreen Driver Setup
```bash
# SSH into your Pi or use a keyboard
sudo apt update && sudo apt upgrade -y

# Install touchscreen drivers (JJN Electron)
# Check your specific model — common driver:
git clone https://github.com/goodtft/LCD-show.git
cd LCD-show
chmod +x LCD35-show  # or LCD3-show depending on model
sudo ./LCD35-show    # This will reboot

# After reboot, calibrate touchscreen
sudo apt install xinput-calibrator
DISPLAY=:0 xinput_calibrator
```

---

## Software Setup

### 1. Install Node.js
```bash
# Install Node.js 18+ on Pi
curl -fsSL https://deb.nodesource.com/setup_18.x | sudo bash -
sudo apt install -y nodejs

# Verify
node --version  # Should be 18+
npm --version
```

### 2. Create the Project
```bash
mkdir ~/nouns-terminal && cd ~/nouns-terminal

# Initialize with Vite + React
npm create vite@latest . -- --template react
npm install

# Install Web3 dependencies
npm install ethers@6 @walletconnect/ethereum-provider
npm install @tanstack/react-query
```

### 3. Deploy the Terminal Code

Copy the `nouns-terminal.jsx` file as your main App component:

```bash
# Replace src/App.jsx with the terminal
cp nouns-terminal.jsx src/App.jsx
```

### 4. Add Web3 Integration

Create `src/lib/contracts.js`:

```javascript
import { ethers } from 'ethers';

// Contract ABIs (key functions only)
const NOUNS_DAO_ABI = [
  "function propose(address[] targets, uint256[] values, string[] signatures, bytes[] calldatas, string description) returns (uint256)",
  "function castVote(uint256 proposalId, uint8 support)",
  "function castVoteWithReason(uint256 proposalId, uint8 support, string reason)",
  "function queue(uint256 proposalId)",
  "function execute(uint256 proposalId)",
  "function state(uint256 proposalId) view returns (uint8)",
  "function proposals(uint256 proposalId) view returns (tuple)",
  "function proposalCount() view returns (uint256)",
];

const NOUNS_DATA_ABI = [
  "function createProposalCandidate(address[] targets, uint256[] values, string[] signatures, bytes[] calldatas, string description, string slug, uint256 proposalIdToUpdate) payable",
  "function updateProposalCandidate(address[] targets, uint256[] values, string[] signatures, bytes[] calldatas, string description, string slug, uint256 proposalIdToUpdate, string reason)",
  "function cancelProposalCandidate(string slug)",
  "function addSignature(bytes sig, uint256 expirationTimestamp, address proposer, string slug, uint256 proposalIdToUpdate, bytes encodedProp, string reason)",
];

const NOUNS_AUCTION_ABI = [
  "function createBid(uint256 nounId) payable",
  "function settleCurrentAndCreateNewAuction()",
  "function auction() view returns (uint256 nounId, uint256 amount, uint256 startTime, uint256 endTime, address bidder, bool settled)",
];

const NOUNS_TOKEN_ABI = [
  "function balanceOf(address owner) view returns (uint256)",
  "function getCurrentVotes(address account) view returns (uint96)",
  "function delegate(address delegatee)",
  "function delegates(address delegator) view returns (address)",
  "function tokenURI(uint256 tokenId) view returns (string)",
];

const CONTRACTS = {
  NOUNS_TOKEN: "0x9C8fF314C9Bc7F6e59A9d9225Fb22946427eDC03",
  NOUNS_DAO: "0x6f3E6272A167e8AcCb32072d08E0957F9c79223d",
  NOUNS_AUCTION: "0x830BD73E4184ceF73443C15111a1DF14e7bdAED",
  NOUNS_DATA: "0xf790A5f59678dd733fb3De93493A91f472ca1365",
};

export function getContracts(signer) {
  return {
    dao: new ethers.Contract(CONTRACTS.NOUNS_DAO, NOUNS_DAO_ABI, signer),
    auction: new ethers.Contract(CONTRACTS.NOUNS_AUCTION, NOUNS_AUCTION_ABI, signer),
    token: new ethers.Contract(CONTRACTS.NOUNS_TOKEN, NOUNS_TOKEN_ABI, signer),
    data: new ethers.Contract(CONTRACTS.NOUNS_DATA, NOUNS_DATA_ABI, signer),
  };
}

// Cast a vote on a proposal
export async function castVote(signer, proposalId, support, reason = "") {
  const { dao } = getContracts(signer);
  if (reason) {
    return dao.castVoteWithReason(proposalId, support, reason);
  }
  return dao.castVote(proposalId, support);
}

// Place a bid on the current auction
export async function placeBid(signer, nounId, amountEth) {
  const { auction } = getContracts(signer);
  return auction.createBid(nounId, {
    value: ethers.parseEther(amountEth),
  });
}

// Create a proposal candidate
export async function createCandidate(signer, { targets, values, signatures, calldatas, description, slug }) {
  const { data } = getContracts(signer);
  return data.createProposalCandidate(
    targets, values, signatures, calldatas,
    description, slug, 0
  );
}

// Fetch proposals from the Nouns subgraph
export async function fetchProposals() {
  const query = `{
    proposals(first: 20, orderBy: createdBlock, orderDirection: desc) {
      id
      proposer { id }
      description
      status
      forVotes
      againstVotes
      abstainVotes
      quorumVotes
      createdBlock
      startBlock
      endBlock
      executionETA
    }
  }`;

  const res = await fetch(
    'https://api.thegraph.com/subgraphs/name/nounsdao/nouns-subgraph',
    {
      method: 'POST',
      headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
      body: JSON.stringify({ query }),
    }
  );
  const json = await res.json();
  return json.data?.proposals || [];
}

// Fetch current auction
export async function fetchAuction(provider) {
  const { auction } = getContracts(provider);
  const data = await auction.auction();
  return {
    nounId: Number(data.nounId),
    currentBid: ethers.formatEther(data.amount),
    startTime: Number(data.startTime),
    endTime: Number(data.endTime),
    bidder: data.bidder,
    settled: data.settled,
  };
}

// Fetch candidates from Nouns Data events
export async function fetchCandidates() {
  const query = `{
    proposalCandidates(first: 20, orderBy: createdBlock, orderDirection: desc) {
      id
      slug
      proposer
      createdBlock
      lastUpdatedBlock
      canceled
      latestVersion {
        content {
          title
          description
          targets
          values
          signatures
          calldatas
        }
      }
    }
  }`;

  const res = await fetch(
    'https://api.thegraph.com/subgraphs/name/nounsdao/nouns-subgraph',
    {
      method: 'POST',
      headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
      body: JSON.stringify({ query }),
    }
  );
  const json = await res.json();
  return json.data?.proposalCandidates || [];
}
```

### 5. Pixel Art to On-Chain Encoding

Create `src/lib/pixel-encoder.js` for encoding pixel art to Nouns-compatible RLE format:

```javascript
// Encode 32x32 pixel art into Nouns-compatible RLE format
export function encodePixelArt(pixels, palette) {
  // Map pixel colors to palette indices
  const indexed = pixels.map(color => {
    if (!color) return 0; // transparent
    const idx = palette.indexOf(color);
    return idx >= 0 ? idx : 0;
  });

  // RLE encode rows
  const runs = [];
  for (let y = 0; y < 32; y++) {
    let x = 0;
    while (x < 32) {
      const colorIdx = indexed[y * 32 + x];
      let runLength = 1;
      while (x + runLength < 32 && indexed[y * 32 + x + runLength] === colorIdx) {
        runLength++;
      }
      runs.push({ length: runLength, colorIndex: colorIdx });
      x += runLength;
    }
  }

  // Pack into bytes (Nouns format: length byte, then color index byte)
  const bytes = [];
  // Header: bounds (top, right, bottom, left)
  bytes.push(0, 31, 31, 0); // full 32x32

  for (const run of runs) {
    bytes.push(run.length, run.colorIndex);
  }

  return '0x' + bytes.map(b => b.toString(16).padStart(2, '0')).join('');
}

// Export pixel art as SVG (for preview/sharing)
export function pixelsToSVG(pixels, size = 320) {
  const cellSize = size / 32;
  let rects = '';

  pixels.forEach((color, i) => {
    if (!color) return;
    const x = (i % 32) * cellSize;
    const y = Math.floor(i / 32) * cellSize;
    rects += `<rect x="${x}" y="${y}" width="${cellSize}" height="${cellSize}" fill="${color}"/>`;
  });

  return `<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="${size}" height="${size}" shape-rendering="crispEdges">${rects}</svg>`;
}

// Export pixel art as PNG data URL
export function pixelsToPNG(pixels, scale = 10) {
  const canvas = document.createElement('canvas');
  canvas.width = 32 * scale;
  canvas.height = 32 * scale;
  const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');

  pixels.forEach((color, i) => {
    if (!color) return;
    const x = (i % 32) * scale;
    const y = Math.floor(i / 32) * scale;
    ctx.fillStyle = color;
    ctx.fillRect(x, y, scale, scale);
  });

  return canvas.toDataURL('image/png');
}
```

### 6. Build & Deploy to Pi

```bash
# Build the production bundle
npm run build

# The built files will be in dist/
# Serve with a lightweight server
npm install -g serve
serve -s dist -l 3000
```

### 7. Kiosk Mode Setup

Create `/home/pi/start-terminal.sh`:
```bash
#!/bin/bash
# Start Nouns Terminal in kiosk mode

# Wait for X server
sleep 5

# Disable screensaver and power management
xset s off
xset -dpms
xset s noblank

# Hide mouse cursor after 3 seconds
unclutter -idle 3 &

# Start Chromium in kiosk mode
chromium-browser \
  --kiosk \
  --noerrdialogs \
  --disable-infobars \
  --disable-translate \
  --no-first-run \
  --fast \
  --fast-start \
  --disable-features=TranslateUI \
  --overscroll-history-navigation=0 \
  --disable-pinch \
  --touch-events=enabled \
  --enable-features=OverlayScrollbar \
  http://localhost:3000
```

```bash
chmod +x /home/pi/start-terminal.sh
```

### 8. Auto-start on Boot

Add to `/etc/xdg/lxsession/LXDE-pi/autostart`:
```
@/home/pi/start-terminal.sh
```

Or create a systemd service:
```bash
sudo nano /etc/systemd/system/nouns-terminal.service
```

```ini
[Unit]
Description=Nouns Terminal
After=graphical.target

[Service]
User=pi
Environment=DISPLAY=:0
ExecStart=/home/pi/start-terminal.sh
Restart=on-failure

[Install]
WantedBy=graphical.target
```

```bash
sudo systemctl enable nouns-terminal.service
```

